body:
Hi,

The current hits widgets only allows to provide a template per hit, I would like to provide a global template so that I can add any HTML attribute I need.

It could make sense to make it overridable with something like:

``` javascript
search.addWidget(instantsearch.widgets.hits({
   container: '#hits',
   templates: {
        empty: '<div class="text-center">No results found matching <strong>{{query}}</strong>.</div>',
        items: '<div class="hits">{{#hits}}Hello {{hit.name}}{{/hits}}</div>'
   }
});
```

What do you think about it?
